  "decisions": [
    "Use an isolated normal clone at the atomically claimed qualified base; preserve the issue226 clone and both immutable read-only discovery records.",
    "Freeze 60 individual public-route cases before behavior edits; capture untouched-original RED with 30 passes and 30 expected ERR_ASSERTION failures, explicit exit 1 and unchanged bindings.",
    "Add only three fresh pairing deadline checks: after approval epoch before write, inside pending branch after rate before return, and after credential hash before consuming approved pair.",
    "Preserve HTTP400 invalid_pairing for approval and HTTP410 pairing_expired for polling; keep initial checks, wrong-code/rate/revocation/device-limit precedence and consume-before-create order.",
    "Reject freshly expired decisions before persisted approval, pair consumption or new device/agent/index/success-audit writes. Allow existing bounded rate bookkeeping and expired-index cleanup.",
    "Use actual signed synthetic Access approval and public gateway/agent routes. Digest barriers await native SHA-256 and prove one selected boundary hit; global fetch is a network tripwire.",
    "Retain positive preexpiry-decision/later-I/O controls. No late postwrite denial, rollback, retry, replay, schema migration, permission or token-format change.",
    "Root owns shared documentation, metric review and publication after issue226; local evidence does not award broader WEB003 or CLI acceptance."
  ],
